  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Discovery Engine: Feature Access Policies & Breaking Change",
  "summary": "This update introduces granular feature access policies for Discovery Engine instances, allowing you to control who can use specific features. A breaking change makes the `verification` field in `EngineFeaturePolicyMember` read-only.",
  "details": "Developers can now define `featurePolicies` directly on `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine` resources (and their alpha/beta counterparts). This new capability allows you to specify `allowedMembers` and `deniedMembers` for individual features, along with a `defaultAccess` setting. Members are defined using the new `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember` schema, which includes `id`, `type` (USER/GROUP), and an optional `displayName`.\n\n**Breaking Change**: The `verification` property within the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember` schema (and its alpha/beta versions) has been made read-only. If your code previously attempted to write to this field, it will now fail. This field is now output-only, reflecting the server's directory check result.\n\nAdditionally, `COMPLIANCE_LEVEL_ITAR` has been added as a new enum value to `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig.complianceLevel`, indicating support for ITAR compliance.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "breaking-change",
    "access-control",
    "feature-management",
    "compliance"
  ],
